WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.095 --> 00:00:13.400
Integrations are the logins and tokens a workstation uses: Claude Code, your git hosts, Jira and MCP servers. They are stored on the workstation itself, never on our server.

2
00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:23.518
Open Integrations in the sidebar. With more than one workstation, you first choose which one. A badge says when something there needs attention.

3
00:00:24.243 --> 00:00:34.920
Each Claude Code account has its own tile. The main account is the one Claude Code itself is signed in with. A second account, here called work, spreads the usage.

4
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:44.604
A tile shows the account, how it signed in and when it was last checked. Test checks the login again, and Remove deletes it from the workstation.

5
00:00:45.305 --> 00:00:54.299
To add one, choose Connect another account. Name it, pick how you want to connect, and Start sign-in. We will cancel here.

6
00:00:55.026 --> 00:01:03.975
Git hosts let the agents push branches and open pull requests. The GitHub tile shows the account and the scopes its token has.

7
00:01:04.676 --> 00:01:10.783
The Jira tile connects your tracker, so agents can read the tickets and attachments behind a card.

8
00:01:11.497 --> 00:01:20.087
MCP servers come with Claude Code plugins. A server that needs a sign-in shows Sign in, which starts the sign-in in your browser.

9
00:01:20.787 --> 00:01:28.622
A server you are signed in to shows Sign out. It asks first, because the sign-in is shared by every pairing on that machine.

10
00:01:29.324 --> 00:01:36.453
That is the Integrations page: every login of a workstation in one place, tested and changed from here.
